==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|G.I.}}

===Etymology===
'''GI''' was originally an initialism for ''Galvanized Iron''; during the 1930s the usage expanded to stand for ''Government Issue''; by World War II it had become a nickname for the military personnel themselves.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|military}} {{initialism of|en|[[general]] [[issue]]}} Given to a soldier by the army (''as'' an item), rather than brought from home; ''or'' used by the army (''as'' a procedure), and different from its [[civilian]] counterpart.
#: {{ux|en|Soldiers counted cadence by chanting: “'''GI''' brush / And '''GI''' comb / Gee, I wish that I was home!”}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} {{initialism of|en|gastrointestinal}}
#: {{ux|en|I was queasy after my upper '''GI''' series, but it far outshone the lower one.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} {{initialism of|en|government issue}}

====Derived terms====
* {{sense|gastrointestinal}} {{l|en|GI tract}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A member of the U.S. military.
# One who is [[demanding]] and [[strict]], in the manner of a stereotypical member of the military.
# {{initialism of|en|[[galvanize|galvanized]] [[iron]]}}
# {{initialism of|en|geographical indication}}
# {{initialism of|en|glycemic index}}
# {{misspelling of|en|Gl}}, the prefix for [[Gliese]] catalog of nearby stars

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|military}} To [[clean]] aggressively.
#: {{ux|en|Top, get the unit to '''GI''' this AO before the old man arrives.}}

